# Third-party notices

## BCC Sans (src/ui/fonts/)

The UI typeface is a subset of **Pretendard** by Kil Hyung-jin (길형진),
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The full licence text is in
`src/ui/fonts/OFL.txt`, and the copyright and licence records are preserved
inside the font binaries themselves.

- Upstream: https://github.com/orioncactus/pretendard
- Version subsetted: 1.309
- Renamed to "BCC Sans" per OFL 1.1 §3, which forbids a Modified Version
  from carrying the Reserved Font Name.

Pretendard itself is built on other OFL work, and that chain is recorded in the
upstream font's own metadata: base glyphs from Inter by Rasmus Andersson;
Hangul glyphs from Noto Sans CJK (Source Han Sans) by Jang Soo-young and Kang
Joo-yeon, Sandoll Communications.

### What was kept

| range | why |
|---|---|
| `U+AC00–D7A3` | Every precomposed Hangul syllable, all 11172. Non-negotiable: nicknames are user input and `NICKNAME_RE` admits the whole block, so a narrower subset renders somebody's name as tofu — a bug that surfaces for one user on one device. |
| `U+3130–318F` | Hangul compatibility jamo. The 51 letters an IME actually emits (`U+3131–3163`) are all present; the 43 absent from this range are archaic letters the source font does not have either. |
| `U+0020–007E`, `U+00A0–00FF` | Latin and Latin-1. |
| `U+2010–2027`, `U+2030–205E` | Punctuation — dashes, ellipsis, the middle dot the UI uses as a separator. |
| `U+2190–2193` | Arrows. |

`U+1100–11FF` (conjoining jamo) was requested and is **absent from the source
font** — Pretendard 1.309 carries 0 of those 256 codepoints. Asking for it would
have been a silent no-op. Korean IME composition on the platforms this ships to
produces compatibility jamo and precomposed syllables, both of which are covered.

### What was dropped

Cyrillic, Greek, kana, CJK ideographs, and Latin Extended beyond Latin-1. That
is where the 1.5 MB source OTF's weight lives; removing it costs nothing this
game draws.

### Weights

Two static faces only — 400 and 700. Not a variable font: this project
rasterises every piece of UI text through canvas 2D, and weight-axis selection
on a variable font is unreliable in WKWebView. `src/core/tokens.js` requests no
weight that is not bundled here.
